{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Like a House on Fire", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A Test of Friendship ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in written and spoken situations and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Causative - Get/Have - Solving Problems", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Causative verbs cause something else to happen. You use a causative verb to show that some person or thing caused something to happen. The subject of the sentence caused the action to happen, but didn't do the action.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the causative verbs <span class=\"italic\">get</span> and <span class=\"italic\">have</span> when you want to make it clear that the subject asked, persuaded or paid someone to do something. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">My boss <span class=\"strong\">had me do</span> an emergency project.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In this sentence the boss asks or persuades you to do an emergency project.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure of the causative is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "have + object + verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Milton <span class=\"strong\">had his son come down</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "or ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + get + object + Infinitive ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">got Cindy to join</span> us as well.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">get</span> when you want to show that you need to work a little harder to convince someone to do something</span>.<br> <span class=\"italic\">Have</span> is a little more neutral and implies that you give someone the responsibility to do something.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We have to get someone to play with us.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I better get the bartender to check the keg.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Milton had his son come down. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I got Cindy to join us as well.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Need + Passive Infinitive and Need + Verb + ing", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use <span class=\"italic\">need + passive infinitive</span> and <span class=\"italic\">need + verb + ing</span> to talk about things that need to be done. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use these structures to focus on the <span class=\"strong\">thing</span> that needs doing, not the person who is doing it. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + Need + Passive Infinitive", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">The dishes <span class=\"strong\">need to be washed</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The subject of the sentence is the thing that needs doing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + need + verb + ing", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">The floor <span class=\"strong\">needs sweeping</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use <span class=\"italic\">need</span> with a gerund (v-ing), it has a passive meaning. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The dishes need to be washed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The tables need bussing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The floor needs sweeping and my tables need to be served.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to cover for", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to replace someone in a duty ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'll get Tanya to cover for you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about self-improvement.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to hustle ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to move or act energetically and rapidly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Now hustle down here.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to lose your mind ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to lose your sanity; go crazy", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I think I'm going to lose my mind.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "worth it", "type": "name"}, {"content": "regarded  as sufficiently good, important, or interesting to be treated or regarded ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: For me, it was worth it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dejectedly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in an unhappy and disappointed way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The coach spoke dejectedly after his team lost the game.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "animated", "type": "name"}, {"content": "full of life and energy", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He speaks in such an animated way.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "on me", "type": "name"}, {"content": "this means that the person speaking will pay the whole amount of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Take a cab. It's on me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner describe the characteristics of a perfect friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Individually, write 200 words on things you could do to become a better friend. Include examples of behavior you would like to change.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about things that need to be done in your analysis.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about solving problems in your writing.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I self-reflect on personal behavior", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I express things I have to get/have to become a better friend. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I analyze things that I need to do in my analysis.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can react to things going wrong and respond to difficult questions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things that need to be done.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about solving problems.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What things would you like to change about yourself? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " How would you go about making these changes?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "How to better yourself!", "type